A Dma whose end goes keeps its channel running.
The controller would go on reaching memory, or feeding a device, its holder no longer holds;
a channel runs only with both its ends.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: dma's channel moves bytes to or from another device than its own
Report: dma's channel runs without both its ends
Witness: fuzz dma-dies-with-pool

diff --git a/kernel/dma.c b/kernel/dma.c
--- a/kernel/dma.c
+++ b/kernel/dma.c
@@ -50,7 +50,6 @@ bool dma_busy(const struct dma *d)
 void dma_drop(struct cap *end)
 {
     struct dma *d = p2v(cap_holder(end));
-    dmac_halt(d->channel);
     d->names[end - d->ends] = 0;
     *end = (struct cap){ 0 };
 }
